```lean
import Poincare.D12.VolumeIBP.Divergence

/-! # Metric integration by parts with compact support (chart level) -/

open scoped BigOperators ENNReal NNReal
noncomputable section
open MeasureTheory Set Function

namespace Poincare.D12.VolumeIBP

namespace ChartMetric

variable {n : ℕ} (G : ChartMetric (n + 1))

/-- The metric gradient `∇_g u`: raised-index vector `(∇u)ⁱ = ∑ⱼ gⁱʲ ∂ⱼu`. -/
def gradient (u : Vec (n+1) → ℝ) (x : Vec (n+1)) : Vec (n+1) :=
  fun i => ∑ j, G.invMatrix x i j * partialDeriv j u x

/-- The Laplace–Beltrami operator `Δ_g v = ρ⁻¹ ∑ᵢ ∂ᵢ(ρ ∑ⱼ gⁱʲ ∂ⱼv)`. -/
def laplacian (v : Vec (n+1) → ℝ) (x : Vec (n+1)) : ℝ :=
  (∑ i, partialDeriv i (fun y => G.density y * G.gradient v y i) x) / G.density x

/-- Pairing in the inverse metric... actually ⟨grad u, grad v⟩_g = ∑_ij g^ij ∂_i u ∂_j v -/
```

Then the main theorem:

```
theorem chart_ibp (u v : Vec (n+1) → ℝ) (hu : ContDiff ℝ 2 u) (hu_c : HasCompactSupport u) (hv : ContDiff ℝ 2 v) :
    ∫ x, u x * G.laplacian v x * G.density x = -∫ x, G.metricInnerInverse? ... 
```

The RHS: -∫ x, (∑ i j, G.invMatrix x i j * partialDeriv i u x * partialDeriv j v x) * G.density x.

Proof structure:
1. Define A := fun x i => ∑ j, G.invMatrix x i j * partialDeriv j v x (i.e., A = gradient v).
2. Define X := fun x i => u x * A x i. X is C¹ compactly supported (u compact support, A C¹).
3. Apply weighted_divergence_integral_eq_zero with ω = ρ: ∫ ∑_i ∂_i(ρ u A_i) = 0.
4. Pointwise: ∂_i(ρ u A_i) = ρ u ∂_i A_i + ∂_i ρ u A_i + ρ ∂_i u A_i (product rule thrice).
5. u Δ_g v ρ = u (∑_i ∂_i(ρ A_i)) = u ∑_i (∂_i ρ A_i + ρ ∂_i A_i) = u ∑_i ∂_iρ A_i + ρ u ∑_i ∂_i A_i.
6. So ∑_i ∂_i(ρ u A_i) - u Δ_g v ρ = ρ ∑_i ∂_i u A_i.
7. ∫ of the difference = 0 - ... => ∫ u Δ_g v ρ = -∫ ρ ∑_i ∂_i u A_i.

