Statement:
```
theorem chart_weighted_ibp (f u v : Vec (n + 1) → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hu : ContDiff ℝ 2 u)
    (hv : ContDiff ℝ 2 v) (hvc : HasCompactSupport v) :
    ∫ x, G.driftLaplacian f u x * v x * Real.exp (-f x) * G.density x
      = -∫ x, G.gradInnerInverse u v x * Real.exp (-f x) * G.density x
```

Proof ingredients:
- ω : Vec → ℝ := fun x => Real.exp (-f x) * G.density x
- hω : ContDiff ℝ 1 ω — exp∘(-f) C¹ (ContDiff.exp of ContDiff.neg hf.of_le) times density C¹.
- X := fun y => fun i => v y * G.grad u y i
- hX1 : ContDiff ℝ 1 X (v C²→C¹, grad u C¹)
- hXc : HasCompactSupport X (support ⊆ support v)
- divergence theorem: ∫ x, weightedDivergence ω X x = 0 — weighted_divergence_integral_eq_zero ω hω X hX1 hXc ✓ (it's a general-weight theorem!).

